  <data name="Pokedex_DiffTitle" xml:space="preserve">
    <value>The differentiator: C# as AI glue</value>
  </data>
  <data name="Pokedex_DiffText" xml:space="preserve">
    <value>The main contribution: C# can run ML models to perform inference. The image-recognition model executes inside the .NET process — no separate runtime required in production. Around it, the same stack delivers the HTTP API, validation, caching and the web UI as a real product, not a demo script.</value>
  </data>
  <data name="Pokedex_CardApiTitle" xml:space="preserve">
    <value>ASP.NET Core API</value>
  </data>
  <data name="Pokedex_CardApiText" xml:space="preserve">
    <value>Receives the image, validates it, and orchestrates the pipeline with async/await and clean contracts.</value>
  </data>
  <data name="Pokedex_CardModelTitle" xml:space="preserve">
    <value>Inference in C#</value>
  </data>
  <data name="Pokedex_CardModelText" xml:space="preserve">
    <value>The ML model runs inside .NET and answers one question — which Pokémon is this, and how confident? No notebook, no sidecar process.</value>
  </data>
  <data name="Pokedex_UseMobileTitle" xml:space="preserve">
    <value>On mobile</value>
  </data>
  <data name="Pokedex_UseMobileText" xml:space="preserve">
    <value>Point the camera at the Pokémon image and get the identification on the spot.</value>
  </data>
  <data name="Pokedex_UseDesktopTitle" xml:space="preserve">
    <value>On desktop</value>
  </data>
  <data name="Pokedex_UseDesktopText" xml:space="preserve">
    <value>Upload a Pokémon from the gallery for recognition.</value>
  </data>
  <data name="Pokedex_CardContractTitle" xml:space="preserve">
    <value>Clean contracts</value>
  </data>
  <data name="Pokedex_CardContractText" xml:space="preserve">
    <value>C# DTOs on one side, JSON schema on the other. The model can be swapped without touching the app.</value>
  </data>
  <data name="Pokedex_CardUiTitle" xml:space="preserve">
    <value>Blazor UI</value>
  </data>
  <data name="Pokedex_CardUiText" xml:space="preserve">
    <value>The very page you're reading: upload, result and confidence, rendered straight from the API response.</value>
  </data>
